const ponder=`<section class="ncert-section" id="sec-12-ponder"><div class="section-header"><span class="section-num-badge">12</span><h2>Points to ponder</h2></div><ol><li>Pressure exists throughout a fluid, not only at its walls; an internal gas layer is in equilibrium because pressure acts on both sides.</li><li>At ordinary conditions, intermolecular spacing is about ten times the interatomic spacing in liquids and solids. Mean free path is much larger: roughly 100 times that spacing and 1000 times molecular size.</li><li>Count both quadratic terms of each vibration: kinetic and potential. One active vibrational mode contributes kBT.</li><li>Air molecules do not settle because their kinetic energy greatly exceeds the gravitational potential-energy change over ordinary room heights. Density is only slightly greater at lower levels.</li><li>In general ⟨v²⟩ is not equal to ⟨v⟩²; the mean of a square is not the square of a mean.</li></ol></section>`;
const levels=[quiz.slice(0,9),quiz.slice(9,18),quiz.slice(18,27)];
